    historyContent: {
      origins: 'Developed as a high-skill extension of standard 3-Card Brag, 7-Card Brag appeared in card rooms as a faster-playing alternative to 9-Card Brag (Crash). It emphasizes the tactical discard of the seventh card to perfectly balance two hands.',
      originCountries: [
        'Great Britain',
      ],
      timeline: [
        'Mid-20th Century: Multi-hand Brag variants evolve in the UK.',
        '1980s: 7-Card variant becomes a staple of high-stakes social gaming.',
        'Present: Popular in British card clubs and as a digital competitive format.',
      ],
      evolution: 'The addition of a seventh card and a muck mechanic allows for much more flexible hand construction than the rigid 6-card or 9-card partition variants.',
      cultural: "Regarded as a game of 'perfect balance', where the ability to split 7 cards into two winning three-card units is the hallmark of a master player.",
    },
    setupContent: {
