          ],
          deckDescription: 'One standard 52-card deck consisting of four suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs), each with thirteen ranks from ace down to two. No jokers; used for seven-card Brag where prials, runs, and flushes are ranked and ace may be high or low in runs.',
          suitDescription: 'Four French suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs). Flushes (seven of the same suit) and running flushes (seven consecutive ranks in the same suit) are ranked hands. Suits do not break ties between equal hand types in Brag.',
          rankDescription: 'Thirteen ranks per suit; for prials the three is the highest rank, then two, ace, king down to four. For runs, ace may be high or low. Standard Brag order: prial of threes best, then runs, then flushes, then pairs, then high card.',
          dealPattern: 'Seven cards dealt clockwise individually.',
          bettingLimits: 'No Limit',
          actions: {},
          handRankingSystem: 'None; specialized Brag hierarchy determines the winning hands at showdown.',
          rankingSystem: 'Brag Partitioning',
          useTrump: false,
          notApplicableReasons: {
            drawConfig: 'Standard 7-card Brag does not include a draw pile or exchange mechanic after the initial partition.',
